<p>If the user authentication settings have been made on the printer, you 
 also need to make the user authentication settings on the printer driver.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you use, this function may not be available.</p>
<h2>What Is User Authentication?</h2>
<p>With user authentication, only users who are registered on the printer 
 or server can print using the printer. You need to make the login user 
 name and login password settings for a user to enable that user to print. 
 Users who are not registered on the printer or server cannot use the printer.</p>
<p>Follow the steps to utilize the <span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication</span> 
 function.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For details about user authentication, see the 
 operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
<li><p>When the user authentication function is used, 
 the user code setting on the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Setup</span> menu 
 of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab becomes invalid.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, open the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="2">
<li><p>On the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> tab, click <span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication...</span> to open the <span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">When you make 
 settings on the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> tab, you 
 must log on as a member of the Administrators or Power Users group.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="3">
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">On</span> for <span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the check box for <span class="Term-Soft">Display [Authentication] Dialog Before Printing</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Display [Authentication] Dialog Before Printing for Windows Credentials</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Encrypt [Login Password]</span>, enter the driver encryption key already set on 
 the printer and click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the 
 printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>On the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> tab, click 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Authentication...</span>.<br/>The <span class="Term-Soft">Authentication</span> dialog 
 box appears.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="9">
<li><p>Select a type of login user name, and then enter 
 a login user name and password that is already set on the printer or server 
 for user authentication.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If you do not 
 enter a valid login user name and login password, printing will not start.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="10">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the 
 printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
